Subject: [PATCH 3/4] web: a 1.85:1 pill sends the size it shows

Why:
The WebUI sent 3840x2072 for both the 3840x2072 and the 3840x2076 label,
and 1920x1036 for both 1920x1036 and 1920x1038. Its IMX585 fallback size
lists had only the cinemate-port driver's 2072 / 1036. So on the original
imx585 driver a 1.85:1 pill asked for a size that driver does not have.
Original Apertar sends each pill's own label (resolutionCommandPayload,
WebControlPage.cpp@upstream-1.6.0). Since the previous commit Core maps a
1.85:1 size to the height the probed driver has, so the page no longer
has to.

What:
resolutionCommandPayload returns each 1.85:1 label's own height. The
fallback lists (used until the probed pool arrives) carry 3840x2076 and
1920x1038b in SDR 12-bit and 10-bit, and 3840x2076 in Clear HDR 12-bit,
as Core's tables do. The Clear HDR 16-bit list keeps 3840x2072 (its RAW16
row is unchanged).

Tested:
check_core.sh both tests: both builds without warnings, 18 host tests pass.
--simulate with headless Chromium: the payloads for 1920x1038 and
3840x2076 carry their own heights and get_state then reads 1920x1038 and
3840x2076; with a fake IMX585 snapshot and no pool, the 1.85:1 size of
Full HD binned and 4K is 1920x1038 / 3840x2076 (SDR 12 and 10),
3840x2076 (Clear HDR 12), 3840x2072 (Clear HDR 16); no page errors.
Needs the camera: on the port driver, click 1.85:1 under Full HD binned and
4K, then get_state width/height read 1920x1036 and 3840x2072
(curl -s -X POST http://<pi>:8000/api/command -d '{"cmd":"get_state"}',
journalctl -u apertar-core -b | grep 'camera configured'). On the original
driver they read 1920x1038 and 3840x2076.

